  "title": "Erdős Problem #1199 — Monochromatic Sumsets in Two-Colorings",
  "statement": "In every 2-coloring $c:\\mathbb N\\to\\{0,1\\}$, does there exist an infinite set $A\\subseteq\\mathbb N$ such that all elements of its sumset\n$$A+A=\\{a+b:a,b\\in A\\}$$\nhave the same color? Equivalently, must there exist an infinite $A$ such that, for all $n,m\\in A+A$, $c(n)=c(m)$?",
